# Time Perspective: AI Personalization Dashboard (2024)

 

A Power BI dashboard that looks at *when* customers engage with AI product recommendations, and whether timing changes their buying behaviour.

 

This was a group assessment for INFO811 Business Intelligence (MSc Applied IT, Wintec). This repository holds my part: the **time perspective**.

 

## Business question

 

Does the month, season or time of day change how customers engage with AI recommendations and whether they buy?

 

## Key findings

 

- **Time changes when customers engage, not whether they buy.** The purchase rate stays close to 60% in every period.

- **Monthly traffic is steady.** October was the peak month with 21,525 interactions, yet the monthly seasonal index only ranged from 0.982 to 1.014 (within about 2% of average).

- **Evenings are busiest.** There were 2.6 times more interactions in the evening than at night, with a similar purchase rate (60.4% vs 60.0%).

- **Clicks drop before the cart.** Click rate (60.3%) is 10.8 points above add-to-cart rate (49.6%), and the gap is the same in every period.

- **Season and time of day matter very little.** The purchase rate varies by only 1.7 points, from 59.3% (spring night) to 61.0% (fall afternoon). The 7-day rolling purchase rate dipped to 58.2% around 19–23 November.

- **Discounts do make a difference.** Discounts of 40% or more lifted the purchase rate to 67.5%, against 55.7% for discounts of 5% or less.

 

## What is on the dashboard

 

- Four KPI cards: total interactions, average daily interactions, purchase rate and the click-to-cart gap

- Monthly interactions with a 3-month forecast (95% confidence interval)

- Seasonal index by month (1.0 = an average day)

- Engagement rate by time of day (click, add-to-cart and purchase rates)

- Purchase rate by time of day and season

- Rolling 7-day purchase rate with anomaly detection

- A key insights panel

- Slicers for season, time of day and month

 

![Time Perspective dashboard](images/dashboard.png)

 

## Data

 

- **Dataset:** Retail AI Recommendation Personalization (250,000 customer interactions, 1 January to 30 December 2024, 31 columns). [Dataset link]

- **Main fields used:** `interaction_date`, `time_of_day`, `season`, `clicked_recommendation`, `added_to_cart`, `purchased_after_recommendation` and `discount_percentage`.

- **Data model:** the main interactions table, a 2024 calendar table, and a small Engagement Type table that lets one chart show three rates.

 

## Main measures (DAX)

 

| Measure | What it calculates |

| --- | --- |

| Total Interactions | Number of rows (interactions) |

| Average Daily Interactions | Total interactions divided by the number of days |

| Click Rate, Add to Cart Rate, Purchase Rate | Share of interactions that were clicked, added to cart or purchased |

| Engagement Rate | Switches between the three rates for the Engagement Type chart |

| Seasonal Index | Average daily interactions in a month divided by the yearly average |

| Click to Cart Gap | Click rate minus add-to-cart rate, in percentage points |

| Purchase Rate Rolling 7 Days | Purchase rate over the previous 7 days |

| Anomaly Point | Flags days when the rolling rate is more than 2.5 standard deviations from its mean |

 

## Tools

 

Power BI Desktop, DAX, Power Query (CSV import) and a custom report theme.

 

## How to open

 

1. Download `INFO811_A3_Time_Perspective.pbix`.

2. Open it in Power BI Desktop (free for Windows). The data is stored inside the file.

3. To refresh the data, point the data source to your own copy of the CSV under Transform data > Data source settings.

 

## Limitations

 

- The data covers one year (2024), so the forecast rests on a single yearly pattern.

- In this dataset each season label appears in every month, so the season results describe the label in the data, not calendar seasons.

 

